  body: "# Child responsibility amount: dated source boundary\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation;
    unreviewed. No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured paragraph links a child
    or qualifying young person amount to responsibility for them, records a new-claim date of 1.2.19,
    and states an immigration-status limitation.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 78549, PDF page 81](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=81)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `d5e17de1d343fc6a6498089897b222a4989914fa53f85af9ddc8c9c05471e2b8`.\n\
    \nThe source-stated date is not the capture date. Tax-credit closure and transfer rules require DMG
    memo 04/24 and other cited material; no transfer outcome is inferred.\n\nThe capture date, the publication
    page's update date and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and
    memos need their own provision, version and applicability review.\n\nMemo references are navigation
    to separately captured source evidence. They do not assert incorporation, supersession or current
    legal validity.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/children
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source expressly relates the additional amount to responsibility for a child or
      qualifying young person, with date and scope conditions retained.
    evidence:
    - page: page/78/0081
      quote: "78549    (See ADM memo 05-24) (see DMG memo 04-24) From 1.2.19, when considering a new claim
        to\nSPC, the claimant’s maximum amount shall include an amount for any child or qualifying young
        person\n\nfor whom they are responsible1. Prior to that date, support for pensioners with such
        responsibility was\n\nprovided by tax credits2.\n\n\nNote: An additional amount is not payable
        for any child/ren who’s immigration status is such that they\nhave no recourse to public funds.\n\
        \n\n                              1 SPC Regs, reg 6(6)(d) & Sch IIA, para 3; 2 WR Act 12; s.33
        & Sch 6, para 6"
      locator: DMG 78549
